{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antiviral, Anti-MRSA, Channel inhibitors", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 76.9% similarity to Androctonus defensin. Activity: Active against Hepatitis B Virus (HBV): HBeAg (IC50 3.95 uM), HBsAg (IC50 = 2.28 uM) and HBV DNA (IC50 = 1.26 uM) in cell culture medium. This is the first scorpion defensin that inhibits virus. In addition, this peptide can inhibit the growth of Gram+ S. aureus AB94004 or ATCC25923 or MRSA (MIC 0.08-0.63 uM), B. subtilis AB91021 (MIC 10 uM), B. thuringiensis AB92037 (MIC 20 uM), M. luteus AB93113 (MIC 0.16 uM), and S. epidermidis PRSE P1389 (MIC 0.31 uM). Similar to neurotoxin, it could also effectively inhibit Kv1.1, Kv1.2, and Kv1.3 channel currents, and its IC50value for the Kv1.3 channel was 510.2 nm. Like classical scorpion potassium channel-blocking toxins, basic residues (K13 and R19) of BmKDfsin4 plays a critical role in inhibiting the Kv1.3 channel (Channel inhibitor) ( Meng L et al., 2016). This is the first invertebrate defensin to block potassium channels. UPdated 7/2021; 11/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "27128943", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Toxins (Basel). 2016 Apr 27;8(5). pii: E124. doi: 10.3390/toxins8050124. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03022", "source_id": "AP03022", "source_numeric_id": "03022", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03022", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A Scorpion Defensin BmKDfsin4 Inhibits Hepatitis B Virus Replication in Vitro", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Antimicrobial, Antiviral", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Mechanism: BmKDfsin4 had been shown to exhibit powerful inhibitory activity against HBV replication by reducing the production of HBeAg, HBsAg, and HBV DNAin cell culture medium and the production of intracellular HBsAg, HBV core protein, HBx protein, and HBV RT.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "[Ref.27128943]HepG2.2.15 cells: CC50= 167.82 μM;##HepG2 cells: CC50= 154.24 μM;##L-02 cells: CC50= 103.77 μM.", "hemolytic_activity_text": "[Ref.27128943]Human erythrocytes: 50% hemolysis concentration was 66.85 μM.", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "27128943", "record_granularity": "source_table_row", "reference_text": "Toxins (Basel). 2016 Apr 27;8(5):124.", "sequence_key": "DRAMP:DRAMP31413", "source_id": "DRAMP31413", "source_numeric_id": "", "source_path": "DRAMP/dramp_downloads_2026-04-02/raw/general_amps.txt", "source_record_id": "general_amps:DRAMP31413", "source_table": "general_amps.txt", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "[Ref.27128943]hepatitic B Virus (HBV): Pharmacological profiles of BmKDfsin4 against HBeAg, HBsAg and HBV DNA on HepG2.2.15 cells(HBeAg: IC50= 3.95 μM; HBsAg: IC50= 2.28 μM; HBV DNA: IC50= 1.26 μM).", "title": "A Scorpion Defensin BmKDfsin4 Inhibits Hepatitis B Virus Replication in Vitro.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "DRAMP"}
